      "message": "Fair on the extra MMIO, let me drop that half of it. What is left is smaller: -EBUSY is already on the line below the BUG(), and cwriter_write already handles a failed submit by rolling back, which is the path the stalled case takes. So this is deleting a line rather than adding a mechanism.\n\nOn self-DoS, I think the invalid HVC address argues the other way. It returns an error and hyp carries on, and this is the one place where a host-controlled input panics EL2 instead of failing the operation.\n\nCould we drop the BUG() and let the -EBUSY return?",
